# .spun update with dir001 and @APP@ in spun.cat, both older than on the
# server. dir001 is first and goes to its directory in spun.cat, never to the
# publisher's suggestion; its DIRTEST.TXT exists, so C at the Overwrite
# question cancels it. .spun prints the message, goes on with @APP@ and
# installs it. mame-dir.sh checks that dir001's line in spun.cat and its files
# are as they were, and that @APP@'s line has the new release.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
put @UPDCAT@ /sys/spun.cat
put @OLD@ /apps/spundir/deep/DIRTEST.TXT
autostart .spun update
autostart PRINT "SPUNDIRDONE"
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 40
noreset 7.5
key 16 c
snap 15 20 25 39
screen 39 Overwrite C:/apps/spundir/deep/
screen 39 dir001 Install cancelled
screen 39 SPUNDIRDONE
